WEBVTT

00:13:28.979 --> 00:13:34.222
and they had a bit more

00:13:34.246 --> 00:13:36.792
control of, sort of, managing their time.

00:13:36.816 --> 00:13:37.991
I could imagine

00:13:38.015 --> 00:13:39.791
if you were working in the buildings

00:13:39.815 --> 00:13:43.103
and you had a bit more
of a direct obligation

00:13:43.127 --> 00:13:45.199
to the members and their needs

00:13:45.223 --> 00:13:49.688
that it may not have felt
like you had as much agency,

00:13:49.712 --> 00:13:51.509
so I can't speak to that as much.

00:13:51.533 --> 00:13:53.000
AG: When I sat down with Adam,

00:13:53.024 --> 00:13:55.279
I was asking him
what WeWork was all about,

00:13:55.303 --> 00:13:56.517
what are his goals,

00:13:56.541 --> 00:13:58.048
what's he hoping to accomplish,

00:13:58.072 --> 00:14:00.479
and he said, "We're selling culture."